- `projects/damen-usj-mall/`
- `projects/aeon-mall-kulai-jaya/`
- `downloads/`
- `contact/`

## GitHub upload

Upload the contents of this folder to the repository root. GitHub Pages will serve each directory `index.html` as a clean path, for example `/products/automatic-smoke-curtain/`.

## SEO before production

Each HTML already has its own title, description, keywords, robots directives, Open Graph/Twitter metadata, canonical tag, and JSON-LD. The canonical tag uses `./`, so it resolves correctly on both GitHub Pages and a future custom domain.

Before submitting the sitemap to Google Search Console, replace `https://YOUR-DOMAIN.com` in `sitemap.xml` and `robots.txt` with the final production domain.

## Company profile PDF

The Downloads page still references `Smoke-Master-Solution-Company-Profile.pdf`, matching the supplied source. Put that PDF in the `/downloads/` folder, or update the href if you want it stored elsewhere.


## Local preview before GitHub

**Extract the entire ZIP first. Do not open an HTML file from inside the ZIP.** Opening an HTML file directly from a compressed archive can cause the browser to receive only that HTML file, so the shared CSS, JavaScript and images cannot be found. The result looks like plain browser-default HTML with broken images.

After extracting the complete `smoke-master-github` folder, open `index.html`. You may also open any nested `index.html` directly. Local `file://` navigation automatically appends `index.html`; GitHub Pages keeps the clean folder URLs.
